      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation keeps dense features first, then partitions all of them into window tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution input into a dense feature field. That field is the carrier the compact thought process can read and update. The window partition turns the field into tokens while preserving the full set.",
